  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 318 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nUpper level ridge begins to move eastward across the CONUS on \nFriday. Will see 850 temps nearing 20 degrees celsius and should\nsee that mix to the sfc with all of western and north central \nNebraska in the upper 70s to low 80s. Friday will be the last \nwell above normal day, ending the week. Heading into the weekend\nwill see a cold front move through on Saturday with \ntemperatures in the mid 50s across the northwest Sandhills and \nfor areas across southwest Nebraska where the front will take \nlonger to pass through, temperatures will reach the upper 60s. \nAs the cooler air mass infiltrates the area with the cold front \npassage on Sunday, much cooler widespread temperatures are \nexpected for Sunday with highs ranging from the upper 40s to mid\n50s. Also as the cold front advances through on Saturday and \nstalls across central Nebraska, then fully passing through on \nSunday, there will be chance for precipitation both Saturday and\nSunday. There will be some moderate instability on Saturday \nacross southwest Nebraska and could see the potential for \nisolated thunderstorms, however at this time the severe threat \nwill be low, but lightning will be a concern. Heading into \nSunday will still see rain shower potential but thunderstorm \npotential is not expected. A few of the models have been showing\nqpf amounts around half an inch to an inch for total weekend \nrainfall, will have to continue to monitor as the we get closer \nto the weekend time period.",
